  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1211 PM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nThe aforementioned ridge will continue to travel east, keeping the \nregion dry and warm. Forecasted high temperatures will be in the 80s \nor near 80 for the remainder of the week and through the weekend. A \nlow pressure system currently entering Northern California will \ntrack east-southeast into Utah by midweek. From there, it will dive \nsoutheast through the Four Corners, and track west and south of the \nPanhandles through the weekend. As it stands, the current track \nkeeps precipitation outside of our region.\n\nModels continue to suggest another trough digging into our area \nmidweek next week, which is a delayed timeframe compared to previous \nmodel runs. A lot of uncertainty is associated with the trough; \nhowever, there is some agreement between the models about the trough \nmaking it into the Panhandles. Exact impacts are unknown given the \ntime frame; however, it is something we'll continue to monitor over \nthe next week.\n\nAbdullayev/Vanden Bosch",
